// Must not compile: "undeclared identifier: io.puts is declared in the library module io;
// add: import io;" -- forgetting the import is the first mistake a newcomer makes, and the
// bare message says nothing about where io.puts lives while the compiler is carrying the
// library that declares it.
//
// tests/compiler/missing_include_quiet.sh is the other half: a name that is in no module
// must NOT get a hint, or the hint becomes noise on every typo.
begin
  io.puts(STDOUT, "hi\n");
end.
